{
  "about": "The file system as one session sees it (filesystem.md): `tree` (paths; a directory ends with `/`, parents are implied), `mounts` (directories that are forge repositories), `grants` (path → level none/ro/stage/commit, covering everything below; the most specific wins; none by default), `floor` (path → the most a session may have there; the most specific applies), `cwd` (the start directory, default `/`), and one `op` on `path`: `level` (the session's level there, and whether it is a passage: at none with something granted below), `list` (the entries the session sees: directories and mounts with `/`, a mount ` [mount]`, an entry at ro in a writable directory ` [read-only]`; directories first, then by name), `read`, `write` (a file), `mkdir`, `rm`, `commit`. Answers `{ok: true}`, `{entries}`, `{level, passage}` or `{error}` with the exact text, naming the resolved absolute path. A path the session cannot see is answered by what the model already knows: by its nearest ancestor that is visible (No such file or directory) or a passage (Access denied) — so a hidden entry and a missing one read the same; creating a name taken by an entry at none is denied. LLeMbas: services/fs.py (the view) with security/access.py (levels and grants); CLI: not run until it has a view of its own (an agent's disk is one level for the whole working directory).",
